<caml:Description xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"><caml:Id>20250SB__077399INT</caml:Id><caml:VersionNum>99</caml:VersionNum><caml:History><caml:Action><caml:ActionText>INTRODUCED</caml:ActionText><caml:ActionDate>2025-02-21</caml:ActionDate></caml:Action></caml:History><caml:LegislativeInfo><caml:SessionYear>2025</caml:SessionYear><caml:SessionNum>0</caml:SessionNum><caml:MeasureType>SB</caml:MeasureType><caml:MeasureNum>773</caml:MeasureNum><caml:MeasureState>INT</caml:MeasureState></caml:LegislativeInfo><caml:AuthorText authorType="LEAD_AUTHOR">Introduced by Senator Ashby</caml:AuthorText><caml:Authors><caml:Legislator><caml:Contribution>LEAD_AUTHOR</caml:Contribution><caml:House>SENATE</caml:House><caml:Name>Ashby</caml:Name></caml:Legislator></caml:Authors><caml:Title> An act to amend Section 2710.5 of the Business and Professions Code, relating to healing arts. </caml:Title><caml:RelatingClause>healing arts</caml:RelatingClause><caml:GeneralSubject><caml:Subject>Board of Registered Nursing: advisory committees.</caml:Subject></caml:GeneralSubject><caml:DigestText><p>Existing law, the Nursing Practice Act, establishes the Board of Registered Nursing to license and regulate the practice of nursing. Existing law authorizes the board, with the permission of the Director of the Department of Consumer Affairs, to form advisory committees to advise the board on the implementation of the act.</p><p>This bill would remove the requirement that the board receive permission from the director to form those advisory committees.</p></caml:DigestText><caml:DigestKey><caml:VoteRequired>MAJORITY</caml:VoteRequired><caml:Appropriation>NO</caml:Appropriation><caml:FiscalCommittee>YES</caml:FiscalCommittee><caml:LocalProgram>NO</caml:LocalProgram></caml:DigestKey><caml:MeasureIndicators><caml:ImmediateEffect>NO</caml:ImmediateEffect><caml:ImmediateEffectFlags><caml:Urgency>NO</caml:Urgency><caml:TaxLevy>NO</caml:TaxLevy><caml:Election>NO</caml:Election><caml:UsualCurrentExpenses>NO</caml:UsualCurrentExpenses><caml:BudgetBill>NO</caml:BudgetBill><caml:Prop25TrailerBill>NO</caml:Prop25TrailerBill></caml:ImmediateEffectFlags></caml:MeasureIndicators></caml:Description><caml:Bill id="bill" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"><caml:Preamble>The people of the State of California do enact as follows:</caml:Preamble><caml:BillSection id="id_9D81B307-13EF-4C85-8E02-4C32A9FD99FB"><caml:Num>SECTION 1.</caml:Num><caml:ActionLine action="IS_AMENDED" xlink:href="urn:caml:codes:BPC:caml#xpointer(%2Fcaml%3ALawDoc%2Fcaml%3ACode%2Fcaml%3ALawHeading%5B%40type%3D'DIVISION'%20and%20caml%3ANum%3D'2.'%5D%2Fcaml%3ALawHeading%5B%40type%3D'CHAPTER'%20and%20caml%3ANum%3D'6.'%5D%2Fcaml%3ALawHeading%5B%40type%3D'ARTICLE'%20and%20caml%3ANum%3D'1.'%5D%2Fcaml%3ALawSection%5Bcaml%3ANum%3D'2710.5.'%5D)" xlink:label="fractionType: LAW_SECTION||version: Added by Stats. 1974, Ch. 632. [id_7925d417-291e-11d9-87bf-bcb27e518802]" xlink:type="locator">Section 2710.5 of the <caml:DocName>Business and Professions Code</caml:DocName> is amended to read:</caml:ActionLine><caml:Fragment><caml:LawSection id="id_96640206-27D4-41AE-970F-81B0AB6B4E73"><caml:Num>2710.5.</caml:Num><caml:LawSectionVersion id="id_D0677ED2-4325-433F-8D75-F0C29CA08F14"><caml:Content><p>The<?xm-deletion_mark data=" board, with permission of the Director of the Department of Consumer Affairs,"?><?xm-insertion_mark_start?> board<?xm-insertion_mark_end?> may form advisory committees to advise the board on the implementation of this chapter. Members of such advisory committees shall be entitled to a per diem and expenses as provided in Section 103.</p></caml:Content></caml:LawSectionVersion></caml:LawSection></caml:Fragment></caml:BillSection></caml:Bill></caml:MeasureDoc>